        "original_id": "d413b6f5-25b2-5636-9c1b-abed9680c4af",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Augusta, Georgia; Savannah River; New Orleans\n- Systems: Augusta Canal; New Orleans Outfall Canals\n- Structures: Butt Memorial Bridge; levees; floodwalls\n- Roads: 15th Street\n\nFacts:\n- The Augusta Canal is fed by the Savannah River and passes through about 13 miles across three levels in suburban and urban Augusta before returning water to the river at various locations.\n- The New Orleans Outfall Canals are lined by 13 miles of levees and floodwalls.\n- The Butt Memorial Bridge is a road bridge in Augusta, Georgia, that carries 15th Street over the Augusta Canal.",
